        "To achieve a locked 60 FPS in real-time games, M\u00fcller introduced Weakly Compressible SPH (WCSPH). Instead of solving a global matrix system, WCSPH evaluates pressure explicitly at every particle using an Equation of State (EOS). Specifically, modern engines utilize Tait's Equation of State: P_i = B * ((rho_i / rho_0)^gamma - 1), where rho_0 is the fluid's rest density (typically 1000 kg/m^3 for water), gamma is the stiffness exponent (typically set to 7 for water), and B is a bulk stiffness modulus that scales with the speed of sound in the simulated medium.",
